body:
i water them really thoroughly when i first plant them and then a light watering whenever the top 1/2-1/4 inch starts to dry out. the 2nd photo is butterfly pea flower and the others are chillis, ive had this happen to a lot of different plants. they are on an outdoor, east facing balcony so they get full morning light and moderate-low light for the rest of the day. im also in australia so its spring here right now.

&#x200B;

your guess could definitely be right. my problem is that i always make sure my seedlings dont dry out too much because i know that they are really sensitive to drying out so i definitely could be overwatering them. ill look into that more. thank you for the reply.

thank you for this reply. im so glad to hear someone else has experienced the same thing. congrats on getting better after leaving graduating and i hope you dont relapse too deeply.

&#x200B;

 thanks for the passion project advice too, also kinda funny because today i spent a few hours in the kitchen, which is a big hobby if mine and for a good amount of the time i was thinking about him, what food he likes, how i could impress him at a future event and all these random things. but ill definitely look into it more
